        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "Assume the model data of [[def-qft-compact-lattice-gauge-data]]. The nonnegative electric operator $H_0=\\lambda_E\\sum_e E_e^2$ is self-adjoint on the stated maximal diagonal domain and finite Fourier/occupation sums are a graph core. The finite plaquette and fermion interaction $V=V_B+V_F$ is bounded and self-adjoint. Therefore $H=H_0+V$ is self-adjoint on exactly $D(H_0)$. Moreover $H$ commutes with every gauge transformation $U(\\alpha)$ on this domain. No continuum-limit assertion follows.",
